# Illustrative ACL for the TEMPORARY Phase 4AA ACL-isolation test only.
# Applies to classic password_file + acl_file brokers. Confirm the broker's
# actual mechanism first; Dynamic Security needs an equivalent role instead.
#
# WARNING: once acl_file is enabled, every authenticated user without a block
# here is denied everything. Add explicit blocks for existing accounts (for
# example Joel's administrative account) BEFORE reloading, or they lose access.
# Do not put general "topic" lines above the first "user" line: they apply to
# all users, including anonymous ones if anonymous access were ever enabled.

# Temporary test device account "brooklynmap" (not the production naming scheme).
# Publish-only: no read and no readwrite lines.
user brooklynmap
topic write brooklyn/v1/brooklynmap/status
topic write brooklyn/v1/brooklynmap/event
topic write brooklyn/v1/brooklynmap/availability

# Existing administrative/observer account must be listed explicitly, otherwise
# it is denied everything once acl_file is enabled.
user goldwein
topic readwrite #

# Read-only collector. No write permission, so it cannot impersonate devices.
user bkmap-collector
topic read brooklyn/v1/+/status
topic read brooklyn/v1/+/event
topic read brooklyn/v1/+/availability

# Production devices (32 lowercase hex username == topic segment) may later use
# a pattern rule instead of one block per device, only after the provisioning
# tool enforces ^[0-9a-f]{32}$ and use_username_as_clientid is verified:
#   pattern write brooklyn/v1/%u/status
#   pattern write brooklyn/v1/%u/event
#   pattern write brooklyn/v1/%u/availability
# A pattern rule applies to EVERY authenticated user, including the collector
# and administrators, so keep it out of the test file.
